Defaulting to --rebase-merges everywhere instead of stopping to ask
was tempting as the safer shape, but it is unproven in combination
with the Step 2 $sha^2 loop under heavy conflicts, and it would bake
in a topology decision the user may not want either. Asking costs one
question; a wrong default costs a reflog dig. The TODO in the message
stands: fold --rebase-merges into the loop shape properly once there
is a conflict-heavy run to learn from.

The trigger uses origin/HEAD..HEAD like the rest of the skill, so it
inherits the existing assumption that origin/HEAD is set - no new
fragility, but no fix for the old one either.

Two data points support the preserved-topology path, but the second
run also hit silent build breaks (see
issues/bulk-catchup-rebase-2026-07-02-2.md). Those are a build-gating
problem, not a topology one, and are deliberately out of scope here -
they belong to the parked --exec change.
